139:Hinana Ichikawa
140:Aha... Where is... One Han City?
141:The four members of noctchill fly to the next stop of their jam-packed tour. When the plane lands, they awake to find themselves in a completely unfamiliar city.
142:Koito Fukumaru
143:I-I can't remember this stop at all... Huh?! You guys, look at the schedule...!
144:The girls gather around Koito Fukumaru and see some strange information on the schedule in her hands.
145:Tour stop, "One Han City." Rehearsal venue, "Mahjong Soul Shrine." Live venue ...Aha? ...Wait, there's nothing written there!
146:Mm-hm... Hm? Wait, no, that's not the point... I could've sworn our next stop and rehearsal venue had different names...
147:Madoka Higuchi
148:That's not all, I'm afraid.
149:Madoka Higuchi waves her phone.
150:It's not working. I can't reach any of the staff.
151:Huh?! H-How is this happening?
152:A strange city, a communication blackout, and a mysteriously altered itinerary... With everyone else left speechless, group leader Toru Asakura stands up, points to a spot on the schedule, and makes her decision.
153:Toru Asakura
154:Either way, let's just go here.
155:This is the Mahjong Soul Shrine? But...
156:Mahjong Soul Shrine
157:But inside the shrine the clues led them to, they're met by a cat-eared priestess...
158:They go up to Ichihime and explain why the four of them have shown up at Mahjong Soul Shrine.
159:Ichihime
160:Nyaa, I understand. Don't worry, this isn't the first time the Mahjong Soul Shrine has received visitors from another world, nyaa.
161:Another world?
162:A talking c-cat...
163:Kaguyahime
164:Hehehe, haven't you noticed yet? This is a completely different world from the one you girls came from.
165:The girls are stunned once again when the girl next to the cat-eared priestess starts to talk.
166:And a talking r-r-rabbit!
167:Hmph. You may be from another world, but you're still just ordinary humans--and with the gall to refer to a deity such as myself as a "rabbit." You shall respectfully address me as Kaguyahime-sama. Understood?
168:U-Understood...
169:A deity? Aha... It's a relief that deities exist here! Excuse me, but could you please send us back to our world?
170:Hehehe, I suppose some humans DO have manners! I could send you back easily, it's just...
171:...Just what?
172:It's just that you're going to be having a live concert in One Han City, nyaa.
173:Wh-Why?
174:Because that's what it says on the schedule, and that's how you'll get back to your own world, nyaa!
175:Sigh...
176:Aha--A live? That's wonderful!
177:But... we're in a different world right now... How are we supposed to pull off a successful show by ourselves in a strange city?
178:We're always performing up on stage... The stage prep, the backstage work... All of this was previously managed by our staff...
179:...
180:???
181:Oh my, so many new faces... Do we have adorable new Jyanshi?
182:Just as silence falls over everyone, a pink-haired girl pokes her head in from outside.
183:It's Kana, nyaa! One Han City's pro idol is here!
184:Kana Fujita
185:Shh! If my manager hears I snuck out to play mahjong, I'll get in serious trouble! {var:ShakeChar}
186:Nyaa, nyaa, nyaa... I'm so dizzy... So many dorayaki are spinning around my head, nyaa...{var:ShakeChar}
187:...Typical reaction for an idol.
188:After taking the head-spinning Ichihime off Kana Fujita's hands, the girls of noctchill fill Kana in on their story...
189:Ooh, I see. No problem, just leave it to me!
190:With a flurry of taps, Kana Fujita confidently sends a form to the girls from her phone.
191:There you go! Everything will go perfectly fine if we prepare according to the marked items in the form.
192:Whoa... "How to Select a Venue," "Marketing Guide," "Makeup and Hairstyle Recommendations," "Concert Equipment Preparation"... This sure is a thorough concert planning guide! One Han City's idol r-really knows her stuff!
193:Haha, it's nothing! I just got some information from the manager with Akane and Mia's help... Hehe... Everything will go perfectly fine if we prepare according to the marked items in the form.
194:"We?"
195:Of course! Idols should always help each other. Just think of me as your tour guide on your otherworld adventure!
196:Thank you so much!
197:We don't have much time, let's divvy up the tasks and get started.
198:After a game of rock paper scissors, the girls of noctchill divide into two groups.
200:Okay!
201:After waving their goodbyes to Ichihime and Kaguyahime, Kana Fujita and the noctchill members leave the Mahjong Soul Shrine to go make preparations for the live concert.
202:Hehehe, what pure, simple children they are! Have they not even considered the possibility that they'll fail?
203:As long as their hearts are in the right place, everything will work out just fine, nyaa!
204:I shall wait and see then.
205:Okay, so Hinana and I will contact the venues. Madoka and Koito, you're on concert promotion and equipment.
